Every unit leaving a production line is examined by three automated inspections. For $i = 1, 2, 3$, let $E_i$ be the event that inspection $i$ rejects a randomly chosen unit. It is known that

- $P(E_1) = P(E_2) = P(E_3) = 0.35$;
- the probability that at least one of the three inspections rejects the unit is $0.70$;
- the probability that all three inspections reject the unit is $0.05$.

Nothing else is known about how the three events depend on one another.

The probability that **exactly two** of the three inspections reject a randomly chosen unit is ________ (rounded off to two decimal places).

